      "id": 4,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"preparation\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Research the main asymptotic bottleneck: replace the per-column bubble sort with a stable O(n log n) sort, then compute the median and mode in one linear scan of each sorted column. Reuse scratch storage where practical. Keep the existing metric formulas and accumulation order unchanged where possible, and preserve the problem’s mode tie semantics; do not rely on the source’s uninitialized mode counter.\",\"B\":\"Explore a no-full-sort alternative: use selection to obtain the required middle value(s) and an exact frequency structure to compute the mode. Match the specified mode tie behavior, including equality handling for doubles, and verify results against the established behavior rather than assuming selection or hashing is automatically equivalent. Compare its measured runtime and correctness with A; do not assume it will be faster.\",\"C\":\"Explore parallelizing independent columns on the ARM64 four-core target. Keep each column’s scratch state private and output columns in their original order. Measure whether parallel work pays off for the tested workload; use a size threshold or stay sequential when thread overhead outweighs the gain. Preserve numerical and output behavior.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only candidates that pass the existing correctness evaluation, and measure each integrated combination rather than adding up individual gains. The run’s baseline is correct on 4 cases, with score 0.5 and mean runtime 0.009294 s (samples: 0.009409, 0.009289, 0.009185 s). Retain the fastest measured correct program; algorithmic and parallel changes may interact adversely. Preserve all seven metric lines, their order, one-decimal formatting, and trailing spaces. Do not specialize to test values or change the tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, or permissions.\",\"analysis\":\"The supplied source sorts each contiguous column using bubble sort and then performs a nested-loop mode calculation, both quadratic in the row count per column. It also makes several linear passes and uses fscanf for all input. Replacing the quadratic work is the strongest source-grounded lead; independent columns also offer a parallelism experiment, though the four-core target and small measured baseline time make threading overhead a concern. The run reports no candidate programs or interaction measurements, so none of these ideas should be treated as a proven gain.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"6f61ac207daca1ec5af375b5f353c3bfda4293af790a4abfd91e30b5a11f014d\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Research the main asymptotic bottleneck: replace the per-column bubble sort with a stable O(n log n) sort, then compute the median and mode in one linear scan of each sorted column. Reuse scratch storage where practical. Keep the existing metric formulas and accumulation order unchanged where possible, and preserve the problem’s mode tie semantics; do not rely on the source’s uninitialized mode counter.\",\"B\":\"Explore a no-full-sort alternative: use selection to obtain the required middle value(s) and an exact frequency structure to compute the mode. Match the specified mode tie behavior, including equality handling for doubles, and verify results against the established behavior rather than assuming selection or hashing is automatically equivalent. Compare its measured runtime and correctness with A; do not assume it will be faster.\",\"C\":\"Explore parallelizing independent columns on the ARM64 four-core target. Keep each column’s scratch state private and output columns in their original order. Measure whether parallel work pays off for the tested workload; use a size threshold or stay sequential when thread overhead outweighs the gain. Preserve numerical and output behavior.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only candidates that pass the existing correctness evaluation, and measure each integrated combination rather than adding up individual gains. The run’s baseline is correct on 4 cases, with score 0.5 and mean runtime 0.009294 s (samples: 0.009409, 0.009289, 0.009185 s). Retain the fastest measured correct program; algorithmic and parallel changes may interact adversely. Preserve all seven metric lines, their order, one-decimal formatting, and trailing spaces. Do not specialize to test values or change the tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, or permissions.\",\"analysis\":\"The supplied source sorts each contiguous column using bubble sort and then performs a nested-loop mode calculation, both quadratic in the row count per column. It also makes several linear passes and uses fscanf for all input. Replacing the quadratic work is the strongest source-grounded lead; independent columns also offer a parallelism experiment, though the four-core target and small measured baseline time make threading overhead a concern. The run reports no candidate programs or interaction measurements, so none of these ideas should be treated as a proven gain.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"nonce\":\"de452386ed53426c856ebe8658e88468\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"max\",\"request_sha256\":\"6f61ac207daca1ec5af375b5f353c3bfda4293af790a4abfd91e30b5a11f014d\",\"session_id\":\"c08531b8446a447bacb06c4500c0c033\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"79789c361c78019edb81003c539a0846880487615ef809beabbcf2245587156c\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":12609,\"output_tokens\":6140,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":5672}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"max\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":18749,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
